00:06:40.928 --> 00:06:42.668
The question in front of a future president

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.348
is whether Donald Trump's new order

00:06:44.348 --> 00:06:46.768
can freeze the Oval Office as a national monument.

00:06:47.188 --> 00:06:49.408
He told reporters the room is a national symbol

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:52.048
and must not be touched, destroyed or ripped down

00:06:52.048 --> 00:06:54.448
so someone can rebuild it in a slightly different shape.

00:06:54.848 --> 00:06:57.628
He said the White House and the office had been badly damaged

00:06:57.628 --> 00:07:00.708
with broken windows, cracked walls, and broken stone,

00:07:00.908 --> 00:07:03.568
and that the order would make destruction of the space impossible.

00:07:04.208 --> 00:07:07.828
The BBC reports the document itself leaves redecorating furniture

00:07:07.828 --> 00:07:10.728
and ordinary security changes in a president's hands,

00:07:10.988 --> 00:07:13.968
so long as they do not substantially harm the historic structure.

00:07:14.648 --> 00:07:17.848
Greg Workheiser of Cultural Heritage Partners told the BBC

00:07:17.848 --> 00:07:20.308
that décor was already the president's to change

00:07:20.308 --> 00:07:22.548
if permanent art and architecture stay intact,

00:07:22.908 --> 00:07:24.728
and he called the order legally meaningless

00:07:24.728 --> 00:07:27.588
because this president cannot tie the next one's hands.

00:07:28.028 --> 00:07:30.628
